{"title":"Career Roadmap · Sanskrit Translator","role":"Sanskrit Translator","summary":"A Sanskrit Translator converts Sanskrit texts into modern Indian languages or English while preserving their meaning, terminology, cultural context, literary style, and historical significance. The career can span classical literature, philosophy, religion, education, publishing, manuscripts, research, digital humanities, localisation, and language technology.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Sanskrit"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Timeline","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Sanskrit grammar, literature and comprehension"}],[{"text":"Skill Building"},{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Translation, interpretation and textual analysis"}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Professional translation + digital tools"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Year 3–4"},{"text":"Translator/Language Assistant"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Sanskrit translation and proofreading"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"3–6 years"},{"text":"Complex texts and specialised domains"}],[{"text":"Senior"},{"text":"6–10 years"},{"text":"Editing, terminology and quality control"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"8–15 years"},{"text":"Translation/project management"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"Research, manuscripts, digital humanities or language technology"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Sanskrit foundation"},{"text":"Grammar, vocabulary, reading"},{"text":"Translation exercises"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Translation capability"},{"text":"Sanskrit → English/Indian language"},{"text":"Translation portfolio"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Professional specialisation"},{"text":"Editing, terminology, CAT tools, research"},{"text":"Internship/project"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Career readiness"},{"text":"Advanced translation + digital humanities/AI"},{"text":"Capstone portfolio"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Sanskrit Language Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong command over:"},{"type":"h","text":"Sanskrit grammar"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sandhi"},{"text":"Samāsa"},{"text":"Vibhakti"},{"text":"Lakāra"},{"text":"Dhātu"},{"text":"Pratyaya"},{"text":"Kāraka"},{"text":"Sentence construction"},{"text":"Verbal forms"},{"text":"Nominal forms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Reading"},{"type":"p","text":"Study texts from multiple categories:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classical literature"},{"text":"Poetry"},{"text":"Drama"},{"text":"Philosophy"},{"text":"Epics"},{"text":"Puranic literature"},{"text":"Dharma literature"},{"text":"Scientific/technical Sanskrit texts"},{"text":"Historical texts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Vocabulary"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"General Sanskrit vocabulary"},{"text":"Philosophical terminology"},{"text":"Religious terminology"},{"text":"Literary vocabulary"},{"text":"Historical terminology"},{"text":"Scientific terminology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Translation Capability"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to translate in both directions where appropriate:"},{"type":"h","text":"Sanskrit → English"},{"type":"h","text":"Sanskrit → Hindi/Regional Language"},{"type":"p","text":"English → Sanskrit can also be valuable for specialised academic and educational roles."},{"type":"h","text":"Translation principles"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literal translation"},{"text":"Sense-for-sense translation"},{"text":"Contextual translation"},{"text":"Literary translation"},{"text":"Technical translation"},{"text":"Terminology management"},{"text":"Cultural adaptation"},{"text":"Annotation"},{"text":"Transliteration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is not simply to replace Sanskrit words with dictionary equivalents."},{"type":"p","text":"You must understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Context","Grammar","Meaning","Cultural reference","Target-language expression"]},{"type":"h","text":"Translation Example Workflow"},{"type":"p","text":"For a Sanskrit passage:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Original text","Text verification","Grammatical analysis","Context research","Draft translation","Terminology verification","Editorial review","Final translation"]},{"type":"p","text":"This workflow is particularly important for classical and philosophical texts where a single term may have multiple contextual meanings."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Translation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop advanced capability in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Literary translation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Poetry"},{"text":"Prose"},{"text":"Drama"},{"text":"Classical works"},{"text":"Commentaries"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Academic translation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research papers"},{"text":"Historical texts"},{"text":"Manuscripts"},{"text":"Scholarly publications"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cultural translation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cultural references"},{"text":"Ritual terminology"},{"text":"Philosophical concepts"},{"text":"Historical terminology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Modern translation"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Government documents"},{"text":"Cultural institutions"},{"text":"Publishing"},{"text":"Museums"},{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"Tourism/cultural content"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Transliteration"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn recognised transliteration systems and their conventions."},{"type":"p","text":"For academic Sanskrit work, develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"IAST"},{"text":"Devanagari"},{"text":"Transliteration consistency"},{"text":"Diacritics"},{"text":"Romanisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Accuracy matters significantly when working with scholarly texts."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation Options"},{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Key Skills","Career Direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"Literary Translation"},{"text":"Literature, style"},{"text":"Literary Translator"}],[{"text":"Academic Translation"},{"text":"Research, terminology"},{"text":"Academic Translator"}],[{"text":"Religious/Philosophical"},{"text":"Philosophy, textual interpretation"},{"text":"Sanskrit Specialist"}],[{"text":"Manuscript Translation"},{"text":"Paleography, textual criticism"},{"text":"Manuscript Specialist"}],[{"text":"Publishing"},{"text":"Editing, proofreading"},{"text":"Sanskrit Editor"}],[{"text":"Government"},{"text":"Official terminology"},{"text":"Language Translator"}],[{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Pedagogy, curriculum"},{"text":"Sanskrit Content Specialist"}],[{"text":"Cultural Heritage"},{"text":"History, heritage"},{"text":"Heritage Language Specialist"}],[{"text":"Digital Humanities"},{"text":"OCR, metadata, databases"},{"text":"Digital Humanities Specialist"}],[{"text":"Language Technology"},{"text":"NLP, linguistic data"},{"text":"Sanskrit NLP Specialist"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Best internship targets"},{"type":"p","text":"Prioritise:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Publishing houses"},{"text":"Sanskrit research institutions"},{"text":"Universities"},{"text":"Cultural organisations"},{"text":"Museums"},{"text":"Digital humanities projects"},{"text":"Libraries and archives"},{"text":"Educational-content companies"},{"text":"Translation agencies"},{"text":"Government language/cultural organisations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship roles"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sanskrit Translation Intern"},{"text":"Research Intern"},{"text":"Editorial Intern"},{"text":"Sanskrit Content Intern"},{"text":"Manuscript Research Intern"},{"text":"Language Research Assistant"},{"text":"Proofreading Intern"},{"text":"Digital Humanities Intern"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong Internship Project"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Sanskrit Digital Translation Portfolio\""},{"type":"p","text":"Select a coherent collection of Sanskrit texts."},{"type":"p","text":"Create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Original Devanagari text"},{"text":"Transliteration"},{"text":"Word-by-word analysis"},{"text":"Grammatical notes"},{"text":"English translation"},{"text":"Hindi/regional-language translation"},{"text":"Cultural/contextual notes"},{"text":"Terminology glossary"},{"text":"Source references"},{"text":"Editorial notes"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Publish selected non-copyright-restricted material in a structured digital portfolio."},{"type":"flow","items":["This demonstrates language competence","translation","research","digital skills."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Certifications and Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Formal certification is less important than demonstrated Sanskrit and translation competence, but additional learning can strengthen employability."},{"type":"h","text":"Translation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Translation theory"},{"text":"Literary translation"},{"text":"Technical translation"},{"text":"Editing"},{"text":"Proofreading"},{"text":"Terminology management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MS Word"},{"text":"Advanced document formatting"},{"text":"OCR"},{"text":"Unicode/Devanagari"},{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Basic XML"},{"text":"Markdown"},{"text":"Version control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Translation technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CAT tools"},{"text":"Translation memories"},{"text":"Terminology databases"},{"text":"Corpus tools"},{"text":"OCR systems"},{"text":"Machine translation"},{"text":"Translation-quality evaluation"}]}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible entry-level roles include:"},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Level"],"rows":[[{"text":"Sanskrit Translator"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Junior Translator"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Language Assistant"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Sanskrit Content Writer"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Sanskrit Proofreader"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Editorial Assistant"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Sanskrit Content Specialist"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Translation Associate"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Language Research Associate"},{"text":"Entry"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Interview Questions"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Why do you want to become a Sanskrit translator?"},{"text":"What is the difference between translation and transliteration?"},{"text":"How do you handle an ambiguous Sanskrit word?"},{"text":"How do you preserve cultural meaning during translation?"},{"text":"What is Sandhi?"},{"text":"What is Samāsa?"},{"text":"How do you verify a Sanskrit source?"},{"text":"How do you maintain terminology consistency?"},{"text":"What is IAST?"},{"text":"How would you translate a philosophical concept that has no exact English equivalent?"},{"text":"How do you handle multiple interpretations of a verse?"},{"text":"What is the role of a commentary in understanding a Sanskrit text?"},{"text":"How would you proofread a translated manuscript?"},{"text":"How can OCR errors affect Sanskrit translation?"},{"text":"Can AI reliably translate classical Sanskrit without human review?"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For long-term professional growth, postgraduate study can be particularly valuable."},{"type":"h","text":"Strong options"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Sanskrit"},{"text":"MA Sanskrit Literature"},{"text":"MA Sanskrit Language"},{"text":"MA Translation Studies"},{"text":"MA Linguistics"},{"text":"MA Comparative Literature"},{"text":"MA Indian Philosophy"},{"text":"MA Ancient Indian History/Culture"},{"text":"MA Manuscriptology"},{"text":"MA Digital Humanities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research route"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Sanskrit","MA Sanskrit","MPhil/PhD where applicable under current university regulations","Research/Teaching/Translation Specialisation"]},{"type":"p","text":"For academic careers, current university and regulatory requirements should be verified because programme structures and eligibility rules can change."},{"type":"h","text":"Government/Public-Sector Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government translation services"},{"text":"Public-sector organisations"},{"text":"Cultural institutions"},{"text":"Museums"},{"text":"Archives"},{"text":"Libraries"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"Education departments"},{"text":"Language departments"},{"text":"Tourism/cultural heritage organisations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential work:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Proofreading"},{"text":"Language research"},{"text":"Cultural documentation"},{"text":"Manuscript preservation"},{"text":"Educational content"},{"text":"Archival documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Government recruitment is position-specific, so verify the current official notification for language, degree, examination and experience requirements."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant postgraduate/research fields include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sanskrit Studies"},{"text":"Indology"},{"text":"South Asian Studies"},{"text":"Classical Studies"},{"text":"Comparative Literature"},{"text":"Linguistics"},{"text":"Religious Studies"},{"text":"Philosophy"},{"text":"Digital Humanities"},{"text":"Manuscript Studies"},{"text":"Translation Studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Potential destinations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"France"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Canada"}]},{"type":"p","text":"International programmes often value a combination of classical-language proficiency + research methodology + digital humanities."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Stage 1 — Entry"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior Sanskrit Translator / Language Assistant"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Translation"},{"text":"Proofreading"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Terminology"},{"text":"Text verification"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 2 — Professional"},{"type":"h","text":"Sanskrit Translator"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Independent translation"},{"text":"Literary texts"},{"text":"Academic texts"},{"text":"Cultural materials"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 3 — Senior"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Sanskrit Translator / Editor"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Complex translation"},{"text":"Quality assurance"},{"text":"Editorial review"},{"text":"Terminology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 4 — Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Language Specialist / Sanskrit Editor / Research Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Textual research"},{"text":"Manuscripts"},{"text":"Publishing"},{"text":"Digital archives"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 5 — Leadership"},{"type":"h","text":"Translation Lead / Editorial Lead / Language Programme Manager"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Translation teams"},{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Quality standards"},{"text":"Publication strategy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 6 — Expert"},{"type":"h","text":"Sanskrit Scholar / Research Director / Language Technology Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route 1 — Literary Translation"},{"type":"flow","items":["Translator","Senior Literary Translator","Sanskrit Editor","Literary Translation Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Classical literature"},{"text":"Poetics"},{"text":"Literary theory"},{"text":"Comparative literature"},{"text":"Style preservation"},{"text":"Cultural interpretation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong literary portfolio is essential."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route 2 — Manuscriptology"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sanskrit Graduate","Manuscript Research Assistant","Manuscript Specialist","Senior Researcher"]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Manuscript reading"},{"text":"Paleography"},{"text":"Codicology"},{"text":"Textual criticism"},{"text":"Cataloguing"},{"text":"Preservation"},{"text":"Digitisation"},{"text":"Metadata"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This route can lead toward museums, libraries, archives and research institutions."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route 3 — Digital Humanities"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sanskrit + Digital Humanities","Digital Text Specialist","Sanskrit Digital Humanities Researcher"]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OCR"},{"text":"Text encoding"},{"text":"XML/TEI concepts"},{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"Corpus creation"},{"text":"Search systems"},{"text":"Text databases"},{"text":"Python basics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A particularly valuable project is a searchable Sanskrit text corpus with transliteration, translation and metadata."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route 4 — Sanskrit NLP / AI"},{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most future-oriented routes."},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Sanskrit","MA/Technical Training","Sanskrit NLP Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Add:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linguistics"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"NLP"},{"text":"Machine learning basics"},{"text":"Unicode"},{"text":"Corpus linguistics"},{"text":"Tokenisation"},{"text":"Morphological analysis"},{"text":"POS tagging"},{"text":"Named entity recognition"},{"text":"Machine translation"},{"text":"LLM evaluation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Possible applications:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sanskrit OCR"},{"text":"Sanskrit search engines"},{"text":"Machine translation"},{"text":"Grammar analysis"},{"text":"Digital manuscripts"},{"text":"Text classification"},{"text":"AI language assistants"},{"text":"Historical text analysis"}]}]},{"heading":"AI & Future of Sanskrit Translation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will increasingly support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OCR"},{"text":"Transliteration"},{"text":"Draft translation"},{"text":"Grammar analysis"},{"text":"Terminology extraction"},{"text":"Text search"},{"text":"Manuscript digitisation"},{"text":"Parallel-corpus creation"},{"text":"Translation memory"},{"text":"Text classification"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, classical Sanskrit requires careful human validation because AI can struggle with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Context"},{"text":"Sandhi segmentation"},{"text":"Multiple meanings"},{"text":"Philosophical terminology"},{"text":"Poetic constructions"},{"text":"Commentarial traditions"},{"text":"Manuscript variants"},{"text":"OCR errors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Therefore:"},{"type":"flow","items":["AI-generated translation","Human Sanskrit expert","Source verification","Editorial review"]},{"type":"p","text":"is likely to be a stronger workflow than unverified machine translation."}]},{"heading":"Sanskrit + Modern Language Technology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A highly differentiated profile can combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sanskrit","English","Linguistics","Python","NLP","Digital Humanities"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Possible roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sanskrit NLP Research Assistant"},{"text":"Computational Linguist"},{"text":"Language Data Specialist"},{"text":"AI Language Evaluator"},{"text":"Digital Humanities Researcher"},{"text":"Sanskrit Corpus Specialist"},{"text":"AI Translation Quality Specialist"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This opens opportunities beyond traditional translation agencies."}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By 2040–2046, Sanskrit professionals may increasingly work across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI language systems"},{"text":"Digital manuscript archives"},{"text":"Multilingual knowledge systems"},{"text":"Cultural heritage digitisation"},{"text":"Computational linguistics"},{"text":"AI-assisted scholarly translation"},{"text":"Digital education"},{"text":"Historical text databases"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential future roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sanskrit AI Language Specialist"},{"text":"Digital Sanskrit Archivist"},{"text":"Computational Sanskrit Researcher"},{"text":"Cultural Heritage Data Specialist"},{"text":"AI Translation Quality Lead"},{"text":"Sanskrit Knowledge Systems Architect"},{"text":"Digital Humanities Programme Director"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Classical-language expertise","translation","research","technology","AI evaluation."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Sanskrit"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advanced grammar"},{"text":"Classical literature"},{"text":"Textual interpretation"},{"text":"Devanagari"},{"text":"Transliteration"},{"text":"Philosophical terminology"},{"text":"Cultural knowledge"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Translation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sanskrit → English"},{"text":"Sanskrit → Hindi/regional language"},{"text":"Literary translation"},{"text":"Academic translation"},{"text":"Technical/cultural translation"},{"text":"Editing"},{"text":"Proofreading"},{"text":"Terminology management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Source verification"},{"text":"Textual criticism"},{"text":"Manuscript research"},{"text":"Academic writing"},{"text":"Citation practices"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unicode"},{"text":"OCR"},{"text":"CAT tools"},{"text":"Digital archives"},{"text":"Metadata"},{"text":"XML/TEI concepts"},{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"NLP"},{"text":"Corpus linguistics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted translation"},{"text":"LLM evaluation"},{"text":"Machine translation quality assessment"},{"text":"AI hallucination detection"},{"text":"Sanskrit NLP"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Experience","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"0–1 year"},{"text":"Translation Intern / Language Assistant"}],[{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Sanskrit Translator"}],[{"text":"3–6 years"},{"text":"Senior Translator / Editor"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Language Specialist / Research Specialist"}],[{"text":"8–12 years"},{"text":"Translation Lead / Editorial Lead"}],[{"text":"12–16 years"},{"text":"Senior Language/Research Manager"}],[{"text":"16+ years"},{"text":"Research Director / Translation Expert / Language Technology Specialist"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an ideal candidate should have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"BA Sanskrit"},{"text":"Strong Sanskrit grammar"},{"text":"Excellent Sanskrit reading ability"},{"text":"Strong English or another target language"},{"text":"Translation portfolio"},{"text":"Devanagari proficiency"},{"text":"IAST/transliteration knowledge"},{"text":"Literary and academic translation experience"},{"text":"Editing and proofreading skills"},{"text":"Terminology-management capability"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"At least one translation/research internship"},{"text":"Digital documentation skills"},{"text":"OCR awareness"},{"text":"Basic digital humanities knowledge"},{"text":"AI-assisted translation evaluation skills"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Profile"},{"type":"p","text":"BA Sanskrit + advanced Sanskrit grammar + strong English/target-language proficiency + translation portfolio + Devanagari/IAST + editing/proofreading + textual research + digital humanities + OCR/CAT tools + AI translation evaluation → Junior Sanskrit Translator → Sanskrit Translator → Senior Translator/Editor → Language Specialist/Translation Lead → Research/Editorial Leadership or Sanskrit NLP/Digital Humanities Specialist."},{"type":"h","text":"1388 | BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours) | Sanskrit | Manuscript Curator"}]}]}